        "original_id": "07ce6f85-9417-5de7-9837-42775125a8c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Adventures of Brer Rabbit, Song of the South, Uncle Remus stories\n- People: Mark Elliot\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company\n- Topics: Br'er Rabbit adaptations, voice-over and trailer narration\n\nFacts:\n- The Uncle Remus stories inspired The Adventures of Brer Rabbit, which exists as a book, a play, and a film.\n- The Walt Disney Company adapted the Br'er Rabbit character for its 1946 animated motion picture Song of the South.\n- During the 1980s and 1990s, Mark Elliot was also the voice of CBS and FOX.\n- Mark Elliot provided voice-over work for theatrical trailers for various non-Disney animated movies, including The Adventures of Brer Rabbit.",
